A||||2||jerpro||94 cavalier transmission in chevy v8 fiero?||||1||
Z||000000||jerpro||05-31-2001||10:39 PM||||As some of you may know. I want to buy a 86gt with a 88 350 v8 in it. While driving it the owner tells me that third doesnt work (auto) and as stated it didn't. When I accelerate and get to second gear it's ok but If I put it in dive the third gear lets loose as soon as I hit the pedal. Third gear stays in as long as you do not acelerate. So to put it up to 70 mph I had to do it in second gear then shift it to 3rd and leave it there.<BR>It has the stock v6 auto tranny in it. <BR>Help!!! as I don't want to buy something that is going to cost too much. He says that he has a 94 cavalier tranny that he can sell me for 200 bucks. Will it work? Is it worth it?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Mach10||05-31-2001||11:17 PM||||If it "drops" down to 2 when you hit the gas, then it sounds as if your kd cable is out of whack, or your valve body's clogged up. Get the KD cable adjusted. I'd also  recommend having your tranny flushed out. If a journal in the valve body is plugged up, then the tranny will shift weird all over the place, and it could manifest itself like you described.||||reg||4
Z||000002||jerpro||06-01-2001||11:52 PM||||thanks. I will keep that in consideration when I go see the car on monday.<BR>thanks||||reg||1
